// RS_Bloom -- CVars
//
// WHY THIS MOD EXISTS.
//
// Bloom is what turns an over-bright pixel into a glow. Every emissive thing in
// this family deliberately writes past 1.0 for exactly that reason -- the neon
// core at 2.6, the white cores in the surface stamps, a wall of light at 2.6
// intensity. None of that reads as LIGHT until bloom picks it up; without it
// they are just pale pixels.
//
// The engine already had the controls, including this fork's own additions --
// a lowerable threshold, a soft knee, anamorphic streaking, a bloom tint and
// chromatic fringing. Not one of them appeared in any menu in this family, so
// the single setting the whole lighting set depends on was whatever it happened
// to be, adjustable only from the console.
//
// EVERY SLIDER HERE DRIVES AN ENGINE gl_bloom_* CVAR DIRECTLY. This mod adds no
// render state of its own -- it is a menu and a set of presets for controls that
// already existed. That is deliberate: bloom is global, one pass, shared by
// every mod, and a second copy of it would be a second thing to keep in step.

server bool rsb_enabled = true;
server int  rsb_preset  = 2;

// Internal. NOSAVE, not server -- see the same note in the sibling mods. A
// server cvar is not written locally when set, so a latch read back next tic
// still reads its old value and the preset re-applies forever.
nosave int  rsb_preset_applied = -1;
